/-!
# The parameter set

Moduli, dropped primes, gadget layouts, the LUT automorphisms, the key layout, and the hash tags of
the generated sparse-LWR claim at this parameter set. The CRT moduli are `Q36 ⊃ Q35 ⊃ ... ⊃ Q1`
(the index counts primes): block `j` of the accumulation multiplies at `Q_(36-j)` and its private
multiplication drops `P_(36-j) = Q_(36-j) / Q_(35-j)`; the readout LUT moves from `Q2` to `Q1`. A
level-`ℓ` encoding at `Q_k` uses the gadget of `Q_(k-1)` re-encoded at `Q_k` with scale `P_k`; the
public vector `a` is encoded at `Q36` with the native gadget and is aligned to the modulus of each
block.
-/

